          "enhanced_information": "It is FALSE that the casein peptides have antimicrobial and immunostimulant activity. While lactoferrin protects against infections by binding iron, cytokines do modulate the immune system in childhood, complex oligosaccharides can mimic receptors for bacteria in the intestine, and lysozyme degrades the cell walls of gram-negative organisms. The evidence supports the role of lactoferrin in interacting with bacteria and the immune system, as well as the general functions of cytokines and oligosaccharides in immune modulation."
